WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.556
- I am a Reform Jew and I have never

00:00:03.556 --> 00:00:06.339
celebrated Christmas. Ever.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.388
- Christmas was not
something I ever learned

00:00:08.388 --> 00:00:10.225
how to celebrate as a young child.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:11.965
- Jesus was born December the 25th.

00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:14.508
And then time started. (laughs)

00:00:14.508 --> 00:00:18.426
(Christmas music)

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:23.043
- All the little kids in the family

00:00:23.043 --> 00:00:24.842
wake up really, really early.

00:00:24.842 --> 00:00:26.293
- Everyone's wearing matching pajamas,

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:28.376
all of the children, and
these are adult children,

00:00:28.376 --> 00:00:30.210
line up in order of size.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.275
And then the parents watch as the children

00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:35.475
run down the stairs and then
everyone goes "Christmas!"

00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:37.258
- I mean, it's just kind of scary, like

00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:38.951
all of a sudden there's all these like

00:00:38.951 --> 00:00:40.243
bells and chestnuts.

00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:41.790
- There's just bells everywhere.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.725
(bells jingling)

00:00:42.725 --> 00:00:44.044
And then they open all the presents.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.713
It's way too many presents.

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:47.076
- at some point during the year

00:00:47.076 --> 00:00:50.769
you have to give your kid
a 200-dollar electronic.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:52.533
Christmas has been set
up to be that thing.

00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:53.783
- And they have the stocking.

00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.735
- But if you get coal in your stocking

00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:57.168
then you're not a bad person

00:00:57.168 --> 00:00:59.152
but your parents are sociopaths.

00:00:59.152 --> 00:01:02.269
- And then the tree dies.
And, uh, Christ was born.

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:03.832
(Christmas bells)

00:01:03.832 --> 00:01:05.406
- Uh, I don't know why you do that-

00:01:05.406 --> 00:01:07.159
I guess to distract
yourself cause you're like,

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:08.852
if you go home you're just gonna be like

00:01:08.852 --> 00:01:10.383
"there's presents,
arghh, like I guess we'll

00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:11.950
"go to church to distract ourselves."

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.334
- Six-year-old girl
playing the Virgin Mary.

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:16.617
- And they like dress up
as donkeys and angels.

00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:20.185
- The children love to dress
up like peppermint sticks,

00:01:20.185 --> 00:01:22.235
and like little Christmas trees.

00:01:22.235 --> 00:01:24.510
- I think that people listen to "hymes".

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.919
- People like wear jeans
to church, I've heard.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.550
- And maybe also just like

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.617
a lot of Mariah Carey Christmas covers

00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:34.635
- Christmas dinner's ham, right?

00:01:34.635 --> 00:01:35.304
- A ham.

00:01:35.304 --> 00:01:37.031
- [Overlapping Voiceovers] Like ham. Ham.

00:01:37.031 --> 00:01:38.381
- Ham, again. I think there's
a lot of ham happening

00:01:38.381 --> 00:01:39.714
- They eat the opposite

00:01:39.714 --> 00:01:41.846
of like what Jews'll eat.

00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:43.874
So they eat like a ham,
you've got pineapples slices.

00:01:43.874 --> 00:01:45.042
- Maybe get a brisket.

00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:46.958
- Then there's like a toothpick
in each pineapple slice

00:01:46.958 --> 00:01:48.157
with a cherry on top.

00:01:48.157 --> 00:01:49.006
- [Voiceover] Yam.

00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:49.992
- [Voiceover] Then there's
gingerbread cookies.

00:01:49.992 --> 00:01:51.291
- You wear like, Christmas hats, right?

00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:53.324
You wear like a Santa
hat? At Christmas dinner?

00:01:53.324 --> 00:01:54.574
- Can you eat mistletoe?

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.523
- In a feat of acrobatics, a fat man

00:01:58.523 --> 00:02:01.545
with a beard and a giant like satchel of

00:02:01.545 --> 00:02:03.293
presents comes down a tiny little hole.

00:02:03.293 --> 00:02:05.208
- Somehow, in the course of one night,

00:02:05.208 --> 00:02:08.657
delivers presents to the whoooole world.

00:02:08.657 --> 00:02:09.872
- He doesn't come to my house.

00:02:09.872 --> 00:02:11.940
Which is weird, like how does he know?

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.539
Like does he see the Mezuzah on the door

00:02:13.539 --> 00:02:16.122
and he's like "ahhh."

00:02:16.122 --> 00:02:19.405
- Santa travels in a
little, like, the wagon,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.377
with the um...

00:02:23.897 --> 00:02:25.348
- Here are the seven reindeer:

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:26.440
Rudolph.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.711
- On Jupiter. On...

00:02:29.711 --> 00:02:30.474
- Snowball.

00:02:30.474 --> 00:02:32.706
- Neptune. They're not,
they're not the Sailor Scouts,

00:02:32.706 --> 00:02:35.753
I don't know their names.

00:02:35.753 --> 00:02:38.392
- One of them's a (beep).
Right? Real mean to Rudolph?

00:02:38.392 --> 00:02:39.293
- [Voiceover] Ew.

00:02:39.293 --> 00:02:40.757
- Is there a "Prancer?"

00:02:40.757 --> 00:02:41.837
- You're like asking me to name the

00:02:41.837 --> 00:02:43.924
back-up dancers on BeyoncĂŠ's tour.

00:02:43.924 --> 00:02:45.076
Can't do it.

00:02:45.076 --> 00:02:50.009
(Christmas music)

